# EcoFlow PowerStream & Smart Meter Automation

An intelligent Node.js control system designed for dynamic zero-export grid compliance (Nulleinspeisung). The script reads live consumption data from a smart meter, calculates the ideal feed-in power via a PID controller, and adjusts the EcoFlow PowerStream inverter in real-time using MQTT. Additionally, all energy metrics are stored in an InfluxDB instance and visualized via Grafana.

## 🚀 Features

- **Dynamic Zero-Export Control:** Real-time adjustment of PowerStream output based on actual household demand.
- **EcoFlow Integration:** Robust MQTT connection to the EcoFlow cloud to monitor solar generation (PV) and battery state of charge (SoC).
- **Energy Monitoring:** Lazy-initialized InfluxDB client for seamless data logging without boot-up race conditions.
- **Grafana Dashboards:** Ready-to-use Flux queries to visualize household consumption, solar generation, and battery status.
- **24/7 Stability:** Optimized for continuous operation on a Raspberry Pi using the PM2 process manager.

## 📋 Prerequisites

- **Node.js** (v18 or higher)
- **PM2** (for background process management)
- **InfluxDB 2.x** & **Grafana**

